==============================================================================
DATA VALIDATION SPL QUERIES
==============================================================================
Use these queries during initial setup to verify the data pipeline is working.
==============================================================================


==============================================================================
QUERY 1: Verify ALL data flowing from the Windows endpoint
==============================================================================
Use this immediately after installing the forwarder. If you see counts > 0,
data is flowing into Splunk.

index=endpoint host=DESKTOP-* OR host=WIN-TARGET
| stats count by sourcetype


==============================================================================
QUERY 2: Verify ALL sources are reporting
==============================================================================
Confirms all 4 Windows Event Log channels are being collected.

index=endpoint host=DESKTOP-* OR host=WIN-TARGET
| stats count by source, sourcetype


==============================================================================
QUERY 3: Verify Sysmon Event ID distribution
==============================================================================
Shows the breakdown of Sysmon event types. Should see lots of EventID=1
(process creation) and EventID=3 (network connection).

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| stats count by EventID
| sort -count


==============================================================================
QUERY 4: Live tail (real-time view of incoming events)
==============================================================================
Use this to confirm events are arriving in real-time as you generate them.

index=endpoint host=DESKTOP-* OR host=WIN-TARGET
| head 20
| table _time, host, sourcetype, source


==============================================================================
QUERY 5: Check forwarder connection health (Splunk internal logs)
==============================================================================
Run this if forwarders look offline. Shows connection status.

index=_internal source=*splunkd.log* 
("Connection to" OR "AutoLoadBalancedConnectionStrategy")
| head 50


==============================================================================
QUERY 6: Verify disk space isn't blocking indexing
==============================================================================
If this returns results, Splunk has paused indexing due to low disk space.

index=_internal source=*splunkd.log* "MinFreeSpace" OR "diskspace"
| tail 20


==============================================================================
QUERY 7: Find all unique hosts reporting in
==============================================================================
Useful when you have multiple forwarders (Windows + Linux later).

| metadata type=hosts
| eval recent_data = if(recentTime > relative_time(now(), "-15m"), "✅ active", "❌ stale")
| table host, recent_data, recentTime, totalCount
| sort -recentTime
